 { Separated passed pawns are also frequent in pawn endings, and there is even a rule saying that when they form a square together with their queening squares, they prove decisive. } 1. { -KEY- } f5 { Creating a square on c5-c8-f8-f5. } ( { a) White wins immediately; e.g. } 1. f5 Ke7 ( { or } 1. f5 Kc6 2. f6 ) 
2. c6 Kd6 3. f6 ) 
 ( { b) On the other hand, } 1. Kb2 $2 { would be a gross error due to } Kc6 { and Black draws. } ) 

